  "alt": "Ink-and-gouache painting of the whole French village seen from high above as one open countryside, with a sky band and snowy mountains at the top, a meandering river and its branching canal crossed by stone bridges, a main road with curving side lanes and footpaths, and fields, hedges, trees and low hills spread between sixteen districts, each a small copy of its own district map: at the far left by the canal boats, the green-domed and onion-domed houses of prayer; the presbytery, blue-spired parish church, twin-spired cathedral and abbey with its kitchen garden; the museum portico with its fountain, weeping willow, brick wing and giant magnifying glass; the campus of tall-windowed schools, glass observatory dome, columned faculty and gear-window school around a canal quay and an autumn garden; the green valley with ski chalet and snowy slopes, observatory, rocky crag, campsite tents, red barn farm with cows, greenhouses, lake jetty and lighthouse beach; the family house with its garage and red car, the stepped alley and the wash-house on the pond; the weighing tower, shop lane, covered market, bakery, repair barn and brocante wagon; the school, clock tower, fountain square and rainbow workshop; the town hall with its flag, palace of justice, post office, fire station and memorial obelisk; the bank, office buildings with a canal island and brick workshops with a wind turbine; the striped café, cake pavilion, chef's-hat restaurant and red phone boxes; the stadium, kiosk, chessboard games hall, conservatory and theatre with masks; the heart-shaped hedge of coloured gazebos, two towers under a rain cloud and the portrait house; the owl pavilion, maze, pumpkin tent, striped mirror tent, circus tops and the bridge over the pond; the doctor's house, pharmacy, hospital with ambulance and herb garden; and the railway station with its green train, globe tourist office, hotel, ship basin, airfield with a small plane, fishing harbour and tyre garage at the crossroads.",
